# Text formatting: Position superscript and subscript in the rule of a styled part.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Text formatting · Superscript and subscript
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: source
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Mono
				Size: 9
				Color: muted
		For style: result
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 14 0
			Typography:
				Size: 14
				Line height: 20
				Markup: markdown
		For style: sup
			Typography:
				Position: superscript
		For style: sub
			Typography:
				Position: subscript
		For style: note-mark
			Typography:
				Position: superscript
				Color: #B3261E
	Section:
		Text: Text formatting
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Superscript and subscript
		Paragraph: A styled part whose rule declares `Position: superscript` or `subscript` is painted at 70% of the size, above or below the baseline, without changing the height of the line. `Position` is only valid in the rule of a styled part.
			Style: intro
		Text: The 1[st]{sup} floor, of 85 m[2]{sup}, emits 12 kg of CO[2]{sub} a year.
			Style: source
		Text: The 1[st]{sup} floor, of 85 m[2]{sup}, emits 12 kg of CO[2]{sub} a year.
			Style: result
		Text: H[2]{sub}O, x[n+1]{sup} and Stxt[®]{sup}.
			Style: source
		Text: H[2]{sub}O, x[n+1]{sup} and Stxt[®]{sup}.
			Style: result
		Text: With more in the rule and in the marks: [a]{note-mark} and **[2]{sub}**
			Style: source
		Text: A red note mark[a]{note-mark} and a bold subscript N**[2]{sub}**.
			Style: result
		Text: The line keeps its height: a paragraph with superscripts in several lines
			Style: label
		Paragraph: Water boils at 100 °C at sea level, and the area of a circle is πr[2]{sup}. The formula of glucose is C[6]{sub}H[12]{sub}O[6]{sub}, and the 2[nd]{sup} and 3[rd]{sup} editions of the manual describe it in the same terms, with the lines of the paragraph evenly spaced.
			Style: sample
